# VS Code Extension Architecture

The Pocket Agent VS Code extension is responsible for capturing chat data from Cursor and facilitating bidirectional communication with the web frontend.

## Core Files

### Main Entry Point
- [pocket-agent/src/cursor-plugin.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/cursor-plugin.js) - Primary extension logic and CDP integration

### Configuration & Utilities
- [pocket-agent/src/config.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/config.js) - Extension configuration management
- [pocket-agent/src/constants.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/constants.js) - Constants including server URLs and GitHub OAuth scopes
- [pocket-agent/src/logger.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/logger.js) - Logging utilities for debug output

### Chrome DevTools Protocol
- [pocket-agent/src/cdpHelper.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/cdpHelper.js) - CDP integration for chat capture and message injection

### Extension Metadata
- [pocket-agent/package.json](mdc:pocket-agent/package.json) - Extension manifest and dependencies
- [pocket-agent/src/extension.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/extension.js) - Extension activation and command registration

## Key Functionality

### Authentication Flow
1. User triggers "Pocket Agent: Sign In" command
2. Extension initiates GitHub OAuth flow via VS Code's authentication API
3. Extension exchanges GitHub token for service JWT with frontend
4. Service token stored for API requests

### Chat Data Capture
1. Extension connects to Cursor's debug port (default: 9223) via CDP
2. Periodically polls all active Cursor windows for chat content
3. Extracts HTML from chat containers using DOM queries
4. Sends data to frontend `/api/chat/update` endpoint

### Message Sending (Web → Cursor)
1. Extension polls `/api/commands/poll-outgoing/[windowId]` for pending messages
2. When messages found, uses CDP to focus Cursor chat input
3. Types message content and simulates Enter key press
4. Handles focus management and error scenarios

### Leader Election
- Multiple extension instances use shared storage to elect a single "leader"
- Only the leader instance performs polling and data capture
- Prevents duplicate requests and data conflicts

## Configuration Options

### VS Code Settings
```json
{
  "pocketAgent.serverUrl": "http://localhost:3000",
  "pocketAgent.debugPort": 9223
}
```

### Environment Variables
- `POCKET_AGENT_SERVER_URL` - Override server URL
- `CURSOR_DEBUG_PORT` - Override Cursor debug port

## Error Handling

- Comprehensive logging to VS Code Output Panel
- Graceful degradation when Cursor debug port unavailable
- Retry logic for network requests
- User-friendly error messages for common issues

## Dependencies

- `vscode` - VS Code extension API
- `ws` - WebSocket client for CDP communication
- Node.js built-in modules (http, fs, path, etc.)

## Security Considerations

- GitHub OAuth tokens securely exchanged for service JWTs
- Service tokens have limited 7-day lifespan
- Extension only sends captured HTML (no sensitive data)
- CDP connections restricted to localhost only




